}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $1$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nFirst, using the addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =5{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(5{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =5{e}^{0} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-101587/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb40a0ff-c3b5-512d-a436-cc2fce456008"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71053/selection/f18d8d958be93720aa6c049f5ce38e8e9b4466e2972d5563b8cedba9c0adeb4f" :answer/id #uuid "06d355e6-3a0a-5c2b-bd66-07d8a5cd6621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)=-2{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71053/selection/d6303427120076b69ad7cfd1e9eb537235db8e5a6f3973d12567f3ac24751ca3" :answer/id #uuid "4dfcddcd-289d-5bcf-bcc8-8db79c6ac8fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)=-{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71053/selection/3a0fec9a170ce5efe4a83dd12ba8a001fc88cf8e0ff03bbe96750cb7c0bc3e5f" :answer/id #uuid "7b88b5e2-fb90-5cbb-8987-6f8497a70025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)=10-{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71053/selection/ad869865697715b8d1897e4ca40cf2e237638fc878084e8b1d89910fff3adcb6" :answer/id #uuid "6c1bc884-e006-5051-bf63-c85a8df7fab6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71053/selection/19d000c1790b0aa483ff055acd65574d7c4fb6ca90658bb1b9865bdf41ed23a0" :answer/id #uuid "22e5d469-e959-5536-b906-dacc240