solution "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $-ln⁡11$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nFirst, using the addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}-ln⁡11) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-ln⁡11) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(2{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1} \\\\  & =2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-101590/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb40a0ff-c3b5-512d-a436-cc2fce456008"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140432/selection/5b3d1610ec0fc75725911e6a93e9e657f7087984f921ba76df15c213d32072ca" :answer/id #uuid "bba20075-83e0-5bbd-bad2-535c7563134d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140432/selection/d03d026bd09fec18424423a8366a5c537953c25f42714aa552e5fb2f8ee77fcb" :answer/id #uuid "2397b92c-fd15-59b5-a1e0-d6fb1b394ffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140432/selection/32505e192a2d4434d2b1b76da1050e4427d675427d6591fb89bcdcea32a24b2b" :answer/id #uuid "20f9a831-647d-5eab-a0a9-6c67c2689274" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+6e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140432/selection/ea1ceecaff49dbd2211415cbc83444a0ca07e70094111f5f7241656bd57ff3f8" :answer/id #uuid "c0c70661-df72-5115-9e5c-f109801e513e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+6e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140432/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "2fdfcb39-e34f-5ef1-a6e5-4c3bbf46379d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140432/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cefc821-2654-5e29-8375-8078e8443fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140432/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-140432/selection/5b3d1610ec0fc75725911e6a93e9e657f7087984f921ba76df15c213d32072ca" "q-140432/selection/d03d026bd09fec18424423a8366a5c537953c25f42714aa552e5fb2f8ee77fcb" "q-140432/selection/32505e192a2d4434d2b1b76da1050e4427d675427d6591fb89bcdcea32a24b2b" "q-140432/selection/ea1ceecaff49dbd2211415cbc83444a0ca07e70094111f5f7241656bd57ff3f8" "q-140432/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140432" :question/id #uuid "10dbaed9-d34d-5103-bc8c-6018b7175763" :question/math-academy-id "q-140432" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}+2x+6{e}^{x}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+2x+6{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2x+2+6{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(2x+2+6{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+2+6\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\  & =2+6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140432/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b7d0153-6e0a-5e19-83f1-960811dc5205"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140432"] :d